**Architecture design (1B dense-equivalent MoE)**

Chosen spec: `hidden_size=1536, num_layers=24, ffn_mult=4` (expert FFN = dense FFN width), `vocab=32000`, `seq_len=2048`, **16 experts, top-k=2, capacity factor 1.25**, aux loss 0.01, bf16.

| Metric | Value | Derivation (calculator formulas) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Dense baseline | **0.955B** | `24·(4·1536² + 3·1536·6144 + 2·1536) + 32000·1536` |
| MoE total params | **11.15B** | `24·(4·1536² + 2·1536 + 16·3·1536·6144) + 32000·1536` |
| Activated params | **1.63B** | `24·(4·1536² + 2·1536 + 2·3·1536·6144) + 32000·1536` |
| Param ratio | **11.7×** | `11.15B / 0.955B` |
| FLOPs/token (train) | **10.1 GFLOP** | `6·1.63e9 + 4·24·1536·2048` |

Routing justification: **Top-2** (default training sweet spot, quality over Top-1); **16 experts** (typical range; total params and all-to-all stay within an 8×80GB EP=8 budget); **CF 1.25** (absorbs routing imbalance without heavy drops); **aux loss 0.01** (strong enough to prevent router collapse at this scale).

**Memory (per GPU, EP=8, micro-batch 4, recompute on):** attention 226.6M + embedding 49.2M + experts `24·2·28.3M=1.36B` = 1.635B params/GPU → bf16 params 3.3 GB + grads 3.3 GB + AdamW mixed `×12` 19.6 GB + activations `24·4·2048·1536·20/2 ≈ 3.0 GB` + ~10%+1.5 GB overhead ≈ **34 GB** (58% headroom on 80 GB).

**Throughput:** 8×H100-80GB ≈ 7.9 PFLOP/s peak; at ~30% MFU (MoE + all-to-all overhead) → `0.30·7.9e15 / 10.1e9 ≈ 235k` tokens/sec. Tokens-per-expert floor: `4·2048·2/(16/8) = 8192` ≫ 8–64. Global batch: `4·128·1 = 512` seqs = 1.05M tokens/step → ~4.5 s/step.

